    {
      "id": 181098,
      "name": "Trajector",
      "username": "Trajector",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-08-14T15:36:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>He’s a fantastic way to make the match easier.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I throw him into matches without regard for difficulty - what I like is how he throws a wrench into things by being different from all the other villains. He’s so single-minded! It’s a terrific implementation of his theme.</p>\n<p>Perhaps one thing I would change about him is to make his initial target selection more random. (Flip a coin to select one of the 2 hero targets with the highest HP?) The way he is now, the players can determine his target just through the game setup selections.</p>",
